title: OK Strategy
subtitle: LO prepares for the biannual class-wide bargaining negotiations.
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: year = 1971 and month == 3
max-visits: 36
frequency: 300
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; 
face-image: img/overenskomst1971.jpg
tags: event

= **[+ next_ok +]**

It is safe to say that the Danish Class struggle is the most instutitutionalized class struggle in the world. 

In the upcoming negotiations LO currently expects to win:
<br>▻ a fourth week of paid vacation.
<br>▻ at least 4% hike in wages.
<br>▻ numerous specific local demands.
[? if oed_support = 1 : <br>▻ the implementation of ØD. ?]

- @learn_more: Learn more
- @discourage: Make LO moderate their demands in order to lighten the pressure on the economy.
- @support_them: Indicate that we agree with their demands.
- @really_support_them: We promise to mobilize our membership and run a campaign in support of the negotiations.
- @encourage_more: Encourage them to up their demands and prepare for conflict.

@discourage
on-arrival: discourage_lo = 1; lo_relations -= 10; b_relation += 9; v_relation += 8; c_relation += 7 if a_in_government != 1; worker_income += worker_income * 0.035; economic_growth -= 0.2;
subtitle: This will upset LO, but it may ease pressure on the economy [? if a_in_government != 1 : and improve our relationship with the governing parties?].
go-to: @unionrelations2 if lo_relations <= 50

Cursewords are exchanged, and a few times we are told to leave the offices. Eventually a compromise, is reached. [? if lo_relations >= 70 : But we are now walking on thin ice.?]

@support_them
on-arrival: support_lo = 1; lo_relations += 4; b_relation += 9; v_relation += 8; c_relation += 7 if a_in_government != 1; worker_income += worker_income * 0.05;
subtitle: This will satisfy LO, but it may put pressure on the economy.
go-to: @unionrelations2 if lo_relations <= 50


The LO leadership is satisfied with our judgement.


@really_support_them
on-arrival: resources -= 1; a_activity -= 0.02; support_lo = 1; lo_relations += 8; worker_income += worker_income * 0.05; economic_growth -= 0.4;
subtitle: - 1 Resource – This will please LO, but it may put pressure on the economy.
go-to: @unionrelations2 if lo_relations <= 50

The LO leadership is pleased with our judgement. Our membership is somewhat distracted over the next few months.


@encourage_more
on-arrival: encourage_lo = 1; lo_relations += 2; b_relation -= 3; v_relation -= 3; c_relation -= 4 if a_in_government != 1; worker_income += worker_income * 0.065; economic_growth -= 0.4;
subtitle: This will please LO, but it may put alot of pressure on the economy [? if a_in_government != 1 : and damage our relationship with the governing parties?][? if a_in_government = 1 : and damage our relationship with the bourgious parties?].
go-to: @unionrelations2 if lo_relations <= 50

The LO leadership is surprised with our decision. Our membership is somewhat distracted over the next few months.


@discuss_next_election


not implemented

@unionrelations2

At the moment our relations with the LO leadership are not good enough for them to want to costrategize with us.

@learn_more


At the bi-annual 'OK' aggreements the working conditions for basically all workers in Denmark are decided upon. The negotiations take place between the confederation of all the Danish unions; LO – and its bourgious counterparts in DI (Danish Industry) and DA (The Danish Employers Organisation). 


- @discourage: Make LO moderate their demands in order to lighten the pressure on the economy.
- @support_them: Indicate that we agree with their demands.
- @really_support_them: We promise to mobilize our membership and run a campaign in support of the negotiations.
- @encourage_more: Encourage them to up their demands and prepare for conflict.